{"tool_name":"cimpleg","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"cimpleg","home":"http://costalab.github.io/CimpleG","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"CimpleG is a simple package to find single-CpG based signatures for use in classification and deconvolution.","addition_date":"2024-01-08T08:24:42.342172Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:22:53.715315Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:cimpleg","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"ivan.costa@rwth-aachen.de","name":"Ivan G. Costa","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2890-8697","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"tiagomaie@hotmail.com","name":"Tiago Mai\u00e9","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"CpG island and isochore detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0430"},{"term":"Deisotoping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3629"},{"term":"Imputation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3557"},{"term":"PTM site prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0417"}]}],"name":"CimpleG","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-023-03000-0","metadata":{"abstract":"DNA methylation signatures are usually based on multivariate approaches that require hundreds of sites for predictions. Here, we propose a computational framework named CimpleG for the detection of small CpG methylation signatures used for cell-type classification and deconvolution. We show that CimpleG is both time efficient and performs as well as top performing methods for cell-type classification of blood cells and other somatic cells, while basing its prediction on a single DNA methylation site per cell type. Altogether, CimpleG provides a complete computational framework for the delineation of DNAm signatures and cellular deconvolution.","authors":[{"name":"Erz M."},{"name":"G. Costa I."},{"name":"Maie T."},{"name":"Schmidt M."},{"name":"Wagner W."}],"citationCount"